# A real vault must never reach the repository. These are the exact on-disk names from
# VaultPaths. Losing this rule means publishing a lawyer's practice to a public repo.
# Tests build their vaults under the system temp folder, so nothing here hides a fixture.
#
# The directory rules are anchored to the repository root. Unanchored, `backups/` matches a directory
# of that name at any depth, which is not only a vault's runtime folder but also
# src/Avocado.Vault/Backups/ and src/Avocado.Server/Features/Backups/. It silently kept the entire
# backup feature out of the repository: commits referenced classes that were never in it, and nothing
# noticed, because it all still built here.
#
vault.json
avocado.db
avocado.db-wal
avocado.db-shm
/blobs/
/backups/
*.blob

